-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Complex Topology:** Highly complex topological structures may be computationally expensive to compute and may not yield clear segmentation benefits [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Attribute Selection:** The choice of topological attributes (e.g., occlusion vs. contour count) significantly impacts the visual result and must be tuned for the specific dataset [S1, unofficial].
+**Edge Cases:**
+- **Degenerate Topology:** Flat regions or constant scalar values may not have well-defined critical points, requiring special handling in the contour tree construction [S1, unofficial].
+- **Precision:** Topological simplification (e.g., pruning small branches) can affect the rendering attributes if not handled consistently [S1, unofficial].
 
